messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: python/libxml.c
Line: 591
Function: libxml_xmlSaveFileTo
Bug type: out-of-bounds-write
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: pyobj_buf is accepted as a generic PyObject and cast to PyoutputBuffer_Object unconditionally to write obj = NULL. If the caller passes a non-output-buffer Python object, PyoutputBuffer_Get(pyobj_buf) returns NULL, but the code still performs ((PyoutputBuffer_Object *)pyobj_buf)->obj = NULL. This writes a pointer into memory of an arbitrary Python object at the offset of the obj field, causing heap memory corruption.

